    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Sharyn McCrumb (born February 26, 1948) is an American writer whose books celebrate the history and folklore of Appalachia.\n[2] McCrumb is the winner of numerous literary awards, and the author of the Elizabeth McPherson series, the Ballad series, and the St. Dale series.\n[3] Paradisbakkerne (\"hills of paradise\"), also Helvedesbakkerne (\"hills of hell\"), is a group of hills in Denmark, located in the east of the island of Bornholm.\n[4] She Walks These Hills is a book written by Sharyn McCrumb and published by Charles Scribner's Sons in 1994, which later went on to win the Anthony Award for Best Novel in 1995."
